            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="0773" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg671"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5747/19–21.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Squiers.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-05-21"><hi rendition="#italic">May 21,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Root instructs Mr. Squiers to give formal notification to the Panaman
                    Government that Mr. Edward C. Bumpus, of Massachusetts, <pb facs="0774" n="672"
                        xml:id="pg672"/> and Hon. Edwin Denby, of Michigan, have been appointed as
                    United States commissioners plenipotentiary on the tribunal for the assessment
                    of land under Article VI of the treaty of November 18, 1903, between the United
                    States and Panama.)</p>
            </div>
